https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-systems/issues/284
Regenerated for ROCm 10.0: upstream inserted a _WIN32 block and further
symbols between hsaKmtAisReadWriteFile and the local: *; terminator, so the
7.1.0 hunk no longer applies. The three exports are still required -- each is
referenced by three files in the 10.0 tree. Anchored on the terminator instead.

hsaKmtCreateQueueV2 added 2026-08-29: rocr-runtime 10.0 calls it (and so does
dev-util/rocminfo, transitively), but upstream never listed it in the version
script. It is defined in src/queues.c with default visibility, so it only
needs exporting. Without this, linking anything against libhsa-runtime64
fails with "undefined reference to `hsaKmtCreateQueueV2'".
--- a/src/libhsakmt.ver
+++ b/src/libhsakmt.ver
@@ -111,6 +111,10 @@
 hsaKmtMemoryCpuMap;
 hsaKmtSetSigbusDelay;
 hsaKmtGetAmdGPUDeviceFd;
+hsaKmtCreateQueueExt;
+hsaKmtRegisterGraphicsHandleToNodesExt;
+hsaKmtModelEnabled;
+hsaKmtCreateQueueV2;
 local: *;
 };
 
